    {
      "short": "Cache costs",
      "chapter": "tradeoff",
      "title": "Cache-aside is simple, not free",
      "body": [
        "<span class=\"term\">Cache-aside</span> is simple but serves stale data up to TTL. Short TTL = fresher data, more misses. Long TTL = better hit ratio, more staleness — and bigger stampedes.",
        "<span class=\"term\">TTL jitter</span> and <span class=\"term\">request coalescing</span> cost nothing and prevent synchronized expiry. There is no good reason to skip them in production."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Redis cache in front of MongoDB",
        "~ Hot-read latency: 2200ms → 60ms",
        "~ Added TTL jitter + request coalescing to prevent stampedes"
      ],
